==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|sv}} {{term|skjóta|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|sv}} {{recons|skeutaną|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sv}} {{recons|(s)keud-|lang=ine-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɧʉːˌta/|lang=sv}}
* {{audio|Sv-skjuta.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{head|sv|verb}}

# to [[shoot]]; to [[fire]]
# {{context|sports|lang=sv}} to [[kick]] a ball or similar; or to [[hit]] it with a stick, in order to attempt to [[score]] a goal in a sport such as [[soccer]], [[football]], [[hockey]] or similar.
# to [[push]] on an object in order to move it; to [[shove]]
# to [[protrude]], to [[extend]] (like a shoot)

